       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, given as up to 800 mg per dose. This order is twice the daily maximum, and each dose is twice the usual maximum single dose.\n- **Risks:** A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,600 mg total per day, split into smaller doses\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale. I'd still want that reviewed with pharmacy first."
