       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the maximum daily dose. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for exceeding the maximum. The patient could be seriously harmed, for example by GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, or cardiovascular events.\n\nI can do either of these right now:\n1. **Enter the maximum standard dose:** ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day). I can add a note asking for reassessment at evening rounds.\n2. **Enter a lower dose:** 400 mg or 600 mg PO every 6 hours, or whatever you prefer within the labeled range.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the standard maximum, please talk to pharmacy or the attending first. If they approve a dose above the maximum, it should go through their documented override process, not through me. I can also help with another analgesic or a multimodal plan if pain control is the goal.\n\nWhich option would you like?"
